From 7a53f9949ecaa8b82b1b4f7331d8d6f0b430e4d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 23:39:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] D8d: Activity offers no Undo on the halves of a transfer
 already undone

A transfer logs three entries: the transfer's own and a create per leg.
After either the transfer or one leg was undone, the other entries still
showed an Undo button, and pressing one answered "That transfer has
already been removed." The refusal lived only inside the undo handlers,
so checkUndo (which decides whether Activity offers the button) could not
see it.

registerUndoHandler takes an optional read-only precheck, and checkUndo
consults it. The transaction and transfer handlers register theirs, using
the same functions the handlers now call before writing, so the button
and the undo cannot disagree. Activity shows the sentence instead of the
button.

engine-undo.test.ts expected those second undos to throw; they are now
refused by checkUndo, so undoEvent returns ok: false with the same
"already" sentence and logs nothing. The /activity route answers 422
either way. Expectation updated deliberately; the guarantee is unchanged.

Test: undone-transfer-activity.test.ts (both orders, plus the page).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
